thogenicity of bovine herpesvirus type 5 in sheep</article-title><source>Comparative Immunology, Microbiology and Infectious Diseases</source><year>1999</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10391508</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0147-9571(99)00008-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mengeling</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><name><surname>Packer</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pathogenesis of chronic hog cholera: host response</article-title><source>American Journal of Veterinary Research</source><year>1969</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>409</fpage><lpage>417</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4179763</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahle</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Liess</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A review on classical swine fever infections in pigs: epizootiology, clinical disease and pathology</article-title><source>Comparative Immunology, Microbiology and Infectious Diseases</source><year>1992</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>203</fpage><lpage>211</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1516362</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0147-9571(92)90093-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Th&#x000fc;r</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Hofmann</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparative detection of classical swine fever virus in striated muscle from experimentally infected pigs by reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction, cell culture isolation and immunohistochemistry</article-title><source>Journal of Virological Methods</source><year>1998</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9763128</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0166-0934(98)00069-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>G&#x000f3;mez-Villamandos</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Garcia de Le&#x000e1;niz</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>N&#x000fa;nez</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Salguero</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruiz-Villamor</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Romero-Trevejo</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>S&#x000e1;nchez-Cord&#x000f3;n</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neuropathologic study of experimental classical swine fever</article-title><source>Veterinary pathology</source><year>2006</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>530</fpage><lpage>540</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16846995</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1354/vp.43-4-530</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bel&#x000e1;k</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Thor&#x000e9;n</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular diagnosis of animal diseases</article-title><source>Expert Review of Molecular Diagnostics</source><year>2001</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>434</fpage><lpage>444</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11901858</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1586/14737159.1.4.434</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Choi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Chae</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Localization of Classical Swine Fever Virus from Chronically Infected Pigs by In Situ Hybridization and Immunohistochemistry</article-title><source>Veterinary Pathology</source><year>2003</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>113</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12627722</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1354/vp.40-1-107</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liebler-Tenorio</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Greiser-Wilke</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Pohlenz</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Organ and tissue distribution of the antigen of the cytopathogenic bovine viral diarrhoea virus in the early and advanced phase of experimental mucosal disease</article-title><source>Archives of Virology</source><year>1997</year><volume>142</volume><fpage>1613</fpage><lpage>1634</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9672623</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s007050050184</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>S&#x000e1;nchez-Cord&#x000f3;n</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Romanini</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Salguero</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruiz-Villamor</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Carrasco</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>G&#x000f3;mez-Villamandos</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A Histopathologic, Immunohistochemical, and Ultrastructural Study of the Intestine in Pigs Inoculated with Classical Swine Fever Virus</article-title><source>Veterinary Pathology</source><year>2003</year><volume>40</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>254</fpage><lpage>262</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12724565</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1354/vp.40-3-254</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>